# Task 2 - where the shuffle is, and what it costs.
#
# climate.csv is a year of room measurements in *long* form: one row per
# reading, as
#     timestamp,field,value
# so a single moment in time occupies three rows — one for co2, one for
# temperature, one for humidity. That is how the sensor wrote it, and it
# is why the first thing any question needs is a step that brings the rows
# belonging together onto one machine.
#
# The question here is per month: within a month, what was the sharpest
# rise in co2 from one reading to the next, and the sharpest fall?
#
# Narrow steps keep each partition where it is. Wide steps cannot, and
# every machine waits for the redistribution. On the diagram a wide step
# is the one with a barrier in front of it.

@machine
class Executor:
    pass

e1 = Executor(speed=1.0)
e2 = Executor(speed=1.0)
e3 = Executor(speed=1.0)      # step 4: make it 0.3

# --- the world -------------------------------------------------------

world = World(machines=[e1, e2, e3])

# --- the pipeline ----------------------------------------------------
# Each line says what it came from. That is the lineage.

readings = textFile("climate.csv")
parsed = readings.map(lambda row: row.split(","))

# Key each reading by the month it belongs to, carrying the hour so the
# readings can be put back in order once they are together.
byMonth = parsed.map(lambda f: (f[0].split("-")[1], (f[0].split("T")[1], f[1], float(f[2]))))
together = byMonth.groupByKey()

# Now every reading for a month is on one machine, so the month can be
# looked at as a whole: keep co2, put it in time order, and measure each
# step from one reading to the next.
deltas = together.mapValues(lambda rs: [b[2] - a[2] for a, b in zip(sorted([r for r in rs if r[1] == "co2"])[:-1], sorted([r for r in rs if r[1] == "co2"])[1:])])
swing = deltas.mapValues(lambda ds: (max(ds), min(ds)))

# step 2: only co2 is ever used, but every temperature and humidity row was
#         carried across the network to get here. Filter to co2 before the
#         pair is built, and read what the shuffle carries now.

job = Spark(pipeline=swing, lose=together)   # step 3: lose=byMonth

world.run(job)
